Frames, trajectories, and other large outputs stay out of git.

Commit code, fixtures of a few KB, and scripts that regenerate or fetch
the data. Large data will live in a Hugging Face dataset repository, or
in DVC. That store is being set up.

Until it is ready, generate the data when the program runs. The OpenMM
reporter test and the overhead script do that: `tests/openmm/water.py`
builds a TIP4P/Ew box, and the dumps and census files are written in a
temporary directory. They are not part of this repository.

Anything placed under `data/` besides this note is generated output and
is ignored.
